#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0127 expect=noViolation domain=SE
#note "JOIN PIN. SE carries subject 002 only and DS carries subject 001 only, so the two share no join key. Match_Datasets [{Keys:[USUBJID], Name:DS}] declares no Join_Type, RulePackageLoader.normalizeJoinTypes stamps INNER, and the unmatched SE rows are dropped before the Check runs -- silent under BOTH the pre-M3-D1 == form and the shipped != form, the only 0127 scenario that is. NOT vacuous for want of data: is_last_in_group resolves over the two SE rows and DSSTDTC is populated; only the join partner is missing. ESCALATE if the harness reports SKIPPED rather than executed-with-no-violation."
#library standard=sendig version=3-0
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col SESTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Element"
col SEENDTC type=Char label="End Date/Time of Element"
---
S1 | SE | 002 | 1 | SCRN | 2020-02-01 | 2020-02-10
S1 | SE | 002 | 2 | TRT | 2020-02-10 | 2020-02-20
---

dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | 001 | 1 | TERMINAL SACRIFICE | 2020-02-15
---
